.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-20 a pre-transaction snapshot that failed on a duplicate name
aborted the apt transaction that was to install Ansible, and with it a
whole Kubernetes cluster's first boot; the hooks warn and go on since.
On 2026-09-26 the hourly snapshots were found never pruned.
.Pp
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: a prune counted a snapshot it could not
destroy as removed; the policy report listed 6,200 lines on a desktop and
called a backup replica over the limit; and a failed snapshot's error was
written to a fixed name in
.Pa /tmp .
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
Nothing takes
.Ql dnf-post
snapshots; the kind exists for the day something does.
.Pp
Fifteen-minute
.Pa /srv
snapshots kept four deep are one hour of history.
Longer is
.Xr sanoid 8 Ns 's
job.
.Pp
Only the running boot environment is snapshotted before a transaction:
a package that writes under
.Pa /home
or
.Pa /srv
is not undone by rolling back.
